# AGENTS.md

## Purpose

Tauri 2 desktop shell for `omp` (oh-my-pi): a Rust backend spawns a verified `omp --mode rpc` runtime per tab, a Bun/TypeScript host (`apps/desktop-host`) wraps it behind a local frame protocol, and a bundler-free React frontend (vendored libs, in-browser Babel) renders chat sessions. Agents optimize for a working offline desktop app with small, tested diffs.

## Source of Truth

1. `CLAUDE.md` — authoritative repo rules: architecture, frontend load order, IIFE rule, god-file caps, gotchas, code style, test policy, changelog/release workflow. Read it before editing anything.
2. This `AGENTS.md` — coding standards and synthesis notes layered under `CLAUDE.md`.
3. `.zcode/memory/project/tech-stack.md` and `.zcode/memory/project/project.md`
4. Code and tests
5. Baseline / external catalogs only when they match this repo's stack

## Stack Snapshot

- **Rust 2021 + Tauri 2** (`src-tauri/`) — process supervision (`agent/`, `process_supervisor.rs`, `host.rs`), git watcher, IPC commands. cargo 1.98, `Cargo.lock` committed.
- **Frontend** (`src/`) — plain JS/JSX, no bundler. Vendored React UMD + `@babel/standalone` transpile in-browser. Script order in `src/index.html` is the dependency graph.
- **Host runtime** (`apps/desktop-host/`) — Bun + TypeScript ESM, `@oh-my-pi/pi-*` 17.4.1 vendored runtime, `bun test` suite, compiles to `artifacts/omp-desktop-host.exe`.
- **Toolchain** — Node 25 / npm 11 (root, only `@tauri-apps/cli`), Bun 1.4 (`apps/desktop-host`), cargo at `~/.cargo/bin` (add to PATH in fresh shells).
- **Detected shape** — desktop app mono-repo: Tauri shell + embedded host runtime + vendored-React UI.

## Core Coding Contract

- Read repo instructions (`CLAUDE.md` first), docs, configs, and nearby code before editing.
- Prefer existing patterns and the smallest correct diff; surgical edits over full-file rewrites.
- Preserve public APIs, data shapes, and external side effects only when they are part of the current requirements — do **not** add backward-compatibility layers, migrations, or fallbacks for obsolete behavior. Delete obsolete code directly.
- Choose the simplest implementation that satisfies the current requirements; no speculative abstractions or config layers. Make a minimal end-to-end version work before adding complexity; never dismantle working code for unfinished complexity.
- Keep components modular with separated concerns; prefer mature, actively maintained libraries; inspect what existing dependencies (`@oh-my-pi/pi-*`, tauri plugins) already do before adding packages or writing custom code.
- Decide for the long term — no "replace it later" temporary solutions. Study how mature products solve the same problem before inventing.
- Do not add dependencies, frameworks, broad refactors, or generated churn unless the task requires them.
- Run the repo's actual formatter/linter/test commands after meaningful changes (see Verified Commands).
- Self-review the diff, including untracked files, and remove debug leftovers before completion.
- Report skipped verification with reasons instead of claiming unverified success.

## Coding Standards (apply strictly)

- **Source:** agent-skills-standard pinned snapshot (https://github.com/HoangNguyen0403/agent-skills-standard, commit `9f695e8e2c3e423dfcd420a0e6b80e0e99044088`, snapshot 2026-08-01, Apache-2.0) — bundled offline fallback; wiki was skipped (no link provided). Re-run `/setup` with a wiki link to upgrade.
- **JS (`src/`):** `const` by default, strict `===`, template literals, guard clauses/early returns, functions <30 lines, no empty catches, throw `new Error()` with descriptive messages — never strings. Comments explain *why*, not *what*.
- **TS (`apps/desktop-host/`):** explicit types on public API params/returns, infer locals, no `any` (use `unknown` + narrowing), no non-null `!`, literal unions / `as const` over runtime `enum`, named exports only, `import type` for type-only imports, async/await with typed `catch (e: unknown)` narrowed before use.
- **IPC boundary:** validate/sanitize every payload crossing Rust↔JS or host↔runtime boundaries; strongly typed shapes; no blocking work inside async Tauri commands.
- **Rust:** no bundled standards pack exists for Rust in the snapshot — `CLAUDE.md`'s Rust rules govern (nightly clippy pedantic+nursery `-D warnings` clean, no `unwrap`/`expect` in production paths, borrow over own, no `.clone()` to bypass borrowck).
- **Reviews / findings:** substance over style; every finding carries file + evidence and severity (`[BLOCKER]`/`[MAJOR]`/`[NIT]`); include test-coverage and edge-case coverage even when CI is green.

## Selected Guideline Packs

- **Strong matches:** `common/common-best-practices`, `common/common-code-review`, `javascript/javascript-language`, `javascript/javascript-best-practices`, `typescript/typescript-language`, `typescript/typescript-best-practices`
- **Medium matches:** `javascript/javascript-tooling` — only its "respect existing tooling, no formatting wars" rule applies; this repo deliberately has no ESLint/Jest pipeline for `src/` (do not introduce one unprompted).
- **Ignored packs:** `common/common-context-optimization` (agent-behavior guidance, not a repo coding rule); `typescript/typescript-security` (no auth/secrets surface in the host); `common/common-accessibility` (no framework UI surface beyond what CLAUDE.md already covers).
- **No exact bundled pack** for Rust/Tauri — repo-local rules in `CLAUDE.md` fill that gap.

## Repo-Specific Rules

1. `omp` RPC contract: spawn `omp --mode rpc`, never `omp --rpc` (falls through to TUI and floods stdout with ANSI). Thinking levels are RPC-driven; valid values `off|minimal|low|medium|high|xhigh` — never invent fallbacks like `auto`/`extended`.
2. Vendor boundary: `@oh-my-pi/*` imports are allowed **only** inside `apps/desktop-host/src/omp-vendor.ts` (enforced by `tests/vendor-boundary.test.ts`). All other modules import from `omp-vendor.ts`.
3. Frontend has no resolver: script order in `src/index.html` **is** the dependency graph — insert new files at the correct point, never append. Every plain (non-Babel) script declaring top-level `const`/`function`/`class` must be IIFE-wrapped: `(function(){ …; window.X = X; })();`.
4. `src/design/` is the live-wired copy; root `design/` is a gitignored read-only prototype. Never regenerate `src/design/` from `design/`.
5. Tests before commit for all non-trivial code: Rust logic gets `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` in-file; host logic gets a `bun test` file under `apps/desktop-host/tests/`. "It doesn't throw" and snapshot/"it renders" checks don't count.
6. Every user-facing change goes into `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` (Keep a Changelog). Release steps are scripted in `CLAUDE.md` — don't improvise.
7. God-file soft caps (~250 lines `.jsx`/`.rs`, ~400 `.js`, ~300 `.css`): split by responsibility when hitting the 6th component or 4th unrelated concern, and update `src/index.html` order when splitting.

## Boundaries / Gotchas

- App must work offline: strict CSP, asset protocol disabled, `tauri-plugin-shell` deliberately removed. No CDN tags, no `convertFileSrc()` without revisiting CSP + capabilities.
- `agent/reader.rs` distinguishes EOF from blank lines and strips CR/LF — don't revert to `reader.lines()` with a blanket `_ => break`.
- `set_model` response must call `notify()` immediately, else the UI reverts on next `turn_start`.
- `omp` must be on PATH (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\omp\omp.exe` on Windows) for dev; the bundled host verifies runtime hashes via `runtime-manifest.ts`.
- Cargo is at `~/.cargo/bin` — not on PATH in fresh Git Bash shells.

## Verified Commands

- `npm run host:test` — 21 tests pass (bun) ✅ verified 2026-08-22
- `cd src-tauri && cargo check --locked` — clean ✅ verified 2026-08-22
- `cd src-tauri && cargo test --locked` — 2 passed, 0 failed ✅ verified 2026-08-22
- `npm run dev` / `npm run build` — Tauri dev/build (GUI; not run during setup)
- `cd src-tauri && cargo fmt` and nightly clippy command — see `CLAUDE.md` (run before commit; not run during setup)
- `node test-rpc.mjs` — probes `omp` RPC (requires `omp` on PATH)

## Code Example

The vendor boundary — the only file allowed to import `@oh-my-pi/*` (`apps/desktop-host/src/omp-vendor.ts`):

```ts
export { SessionManager } from "@oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent/session/session-manager";
export { listSessionsReadOnly } from "@oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent/session/session-listing";
export type { SessionInfo } from "@oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent/session/session-listing";
export {
  MAX_RPC_FRAME_BYTES,
  MAX_RPC_REASSEMBLED_BYTES,
  RpcFrameDecoder
} from "@oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent/modes/rpc/rpc-frame";
```

